From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: restore Trek Tech movie sprite dimensions

The exterior location has no 03WbegQ.mov.  Its missing opening wireframe can
leave puppet sprite 19 carrying stale stretched dimensions when the valid
08WendQ.mov destination movie is assigned, rendering that movie as vertical
strips.

Trek Tech uses sprite 19 for 180x155 wireframe movies and sprite 23 for the
shared detail/transit movie.  Either puppet sprite can retain stale stretched
dimensions when its cast is replaced.  Clear the stale stretch state before
assigning a digital-video cast, then restore the native dimensions after
setCast has loaded the movie and learned its actual size.  This retains each
sprite's authored centre and stage position.  Other sprites, games, videos,
and custom puppet sizing are unchanged.
---
 engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
--- a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
@@ -1926,6 +1926,18 @@ void Lingo::setTheSprite(Datum &id1, int field, Datum &d) {
 			// Since Digital Video dimensions get clarified after loading,
 			// we enforce them here
 			if (castId != sprite->_castId || (castMember && castMember->_type == kCastDigitalVideo)) {
+				// Trek Tech authors its wireframe (sprite 19) and shared detail/
+				// transit movie (sprite 23) at native size. Both puppet sprites can
+				// otherwise carry stale stretched dimensions into the next movie.
+				// The movie's true dimensions are not available until setCast loads
+				// it, so reset these dedicated sprites before and after assignment.
+				bool resetTrekTechVideoSize = (id == 19 || id == 23) && castMember &&
+						castMember->_type == kCastDigitalVideo &&
+						Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech");
+				if (resetTrekTechVideoSize)
+					sprite->_stretch = false;
 				channel->setCast(castId);
+				if (resetTrekTechVideoSize)
+					channel->setStretch(false);
 			}
 		}
